  data:  # 674c
    kind: invariant  # 674c
    title: "io_boundary is a 'canonical risk taxonomy' that consumers branch on, with no declared axis: absent from _known_axes(), no registry, no axiom, no drift linter"  # 674c
    status: violated  # 674c
    priority: 2  # 674c
    parent:  # 674c
    tags:  # 674c
    - catalogue  # 674c
    - io_boundary  # 674c
    - axis  # 674c
    isbefore: []  # 674c
    duplicate_of: []  # 674c
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 674c
    pr_ref:  # 674c
    description: "FILED BY ADR-0049 §\"Open work\". This is the ROOT CAUSE of why WI-johuk existed at\nall, stated separately because ADR-0049 is a value-level ruling that does not wait\non it.\n\nTHE FACT. `_known_axes()` lists edge-type, symbol-kind, evidence-type, language,\npass-id, protocol-origin, qualified-name, entrypoint-kind, visibility. `io-boundary`\nis ABSENT. There is no registry module, no one-sentence axiom, no drift linter, no\nAXIS_* name -- while ADR-0016 and taint.py BOTH call it \"hypergumbo's canonical\nI/O-boundary risk taxonomy\", and while several consumers branch on its values\n(AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP mints taint sources from three of them; OPAQUE_BOUNDARIES\nwithholds confirmations on one; _DISCLOSED_ONLY_BOUNDARIES excludes two from the\nheadline; verify-claims validates claim constraints against KNOWN_IO_BOUNDARIES).\n\nWHY IT MATTERS, AS MEASURED HISTORY RATHER THAN PRINCIPLE:\n  * INV-tutar. `env_read` carried TWO readings -- ambient configuration and secret\n    material -- and AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP read the wrong one. 134 of 195 shipped\n    env_read rows were host DESCRIPTION (runtime.GOOS, os.uname,\n    navigator.platform) or user identity (os.getlogin, pwd.getpwnam). Calling\n    those a secret is why host-secret-* claims carried 48 of 85 adjudicated flows\n    at 22.9% precision, the weakest family in measurement 0001. The catalogue was\n    already distorting itself to cope: python.yaml deliberately WITHHELD getpid\n    and cpu_count because rowing them \"would manufacture false sources\", while\n    go.yaml rowed GOOS and Getwd. One boundary value, two membership rules, two\n    shipped files.\n  * WI-johuk. The server-launch question was derived four times over five months\n    and ruled zero times, because there was no place a ruling could live. The only\n    governing text was a TEST DOCSTRING. Four independent censuses of the affected\n    rows produced four different numbers (37 / 52 / 63 / 75) because there was no\n    membership rule to count against.\n\nBoth are the same failure: a vocabulary that consumers branch on, with no axiom\nsaying what its values mean, drifts one row at a time and has nowhere to record a\ncorrection.\n\nWHAT TO DO (ADR-0024 four-artifact scaffolding, heavyweight):\n  1. a registry module mirroring edge_types.py, with the one-sentence axiom --\n     ADR-0049 ruling 1 is the candidate: a boundary value names WHAT DATA CROSSES\n     THE PROCESS BOUNDARY AT THIS CALL SITE, IN WHICH DIRECTION -- not what the\n     program is thereby arranged to do later;\n  2. a consumer helper;\n  3. a drift linter (parameterise scripts/check-edge-type-drift);\n  4. a runtime property test.\nThen wire io-boundary into _known_axes().\n\nSEQUENCING NOTE: this is a large PR and should land BEFORE the row moves, not\nafter -- otherwise the census (WI-hazop) and the retag (WI-nosah) are once again\nrecorded in prose that the next re-derivation is free to reinterpret. It is\nindependent of ADR-0049 itself, which stands as a value-level ruling either way."  # 674c
    fields:  # 674c
      statement: "Every multi-value vocabulary that consumers branch on must have a declared axis with a one-sentence axiom and a drift linter (ADR-0024); io_boundary has neither, while AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP, OPAQUE_BOUNDARIES, _DISCLOSED_ONLY_BOUNDARIES and verify-claims all branch on its values."  # 674c
      root_cause: "The boundary vocabulary predates ADR-0024 and was never retrofitted, so there is no axiom stating what a boundary value means and no place a per-value ruling can be recorded. Measured consequences: INV-tutar (env_read carried two readings; 134 of 195 rows misclassified; 22.9% precision on host-secret claims) and WI-johuk (the same question derived four times over five months, ruled zero times, four incompatible censuses)."  # 674c
- op: discuss  # 0e7d
  at: '2026-09-01T19:16:46Z'  # 0e7d
  by: agent  # 0e7d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0e7d
  clock: 2  # 0e7d
  nonce: 0e7d  # 0e7d
  message: "OWNER RULING (2026-09-01) on the sibling WI-livar: option (a), DECLARE THE AXIS,\nand INV-tafig is scoped TOGETHER with it. This item is no longer waiting on\nanything -- it is now half of one campaign.\n\nWHY THE TWO SHARE A ROOT AND NOT JUST A SHAPE. This item says io_boundary is\nabsent from _known_axes(). Verified, and the reason is structural rather than\noversight: multi_value_field_axis.DEFAULT_CORE_FILES is exactly ir.py and\ndatamodels.py, while IoPrimitive lives in io_boundary.py. So IoPrimitive.boundary\ncarries no axis comment and nothing ever asked it for one -- the linter cannot\nsee the file. The identical fact hides WI-livar's IoPrimitive.module. One scope\nfix un-hides both, and it is the gate that would have caught each of them.\n\nTHE TWO AXES ARE DIFFERENT SHAPES, WHICH IS WHY THIS IS TWO REGISTRIES AND NOT\nONE. io-boundary is ENUMERABLE -- CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES is 17 values,\nKNOWN_IO_BOUNDARIES adds external_potential and command_launch for 19 -- so it\ntakes the heavyweight edge_types.py registry: AXIS_* constants, an IoBoundarySpec\nfrozen dataclass carrying name + axis + description, the tuple of specs,\nall_io_boundary_names() / io_boundaries_on_axis() / find_io_boundary().\nThe module key is NOT enumerable and takes the qualified_name_axis.py structural-\npolicy shape instead (ADR-0024 section 4 \"use judgment\").\n\nAXIOM CANDIDATE, as this item proposes and ADR-0049 ruling 1 supplies: a boundary\nvalue names WHAT DATA CROSSES THE PROCESS BOUNDARY AT THIS CALL SITE, IN WHICH\nDIRECTION -- not what the program is thereby arranged to do later. Adopting it\nverbatim keeps ADR-0049 the value-level ruling and this the axis that ruling\nlives on. It is falsifiable in the ADR-0024 sense: it is what makes net_listen a\ndisclosure rather than a crossing, and it is the sentence env_read failed when\nINV-tutar found 134 of 195 rows were host DESCRIPTION rather than secret\nmaterial.\n\nSEQUENCING, honouring this item's own note that the axis lands BEFORE the row\nmoves: the registry ships first, then the census (WI-hazop) and the retag\n(WI-nosah) are recorded against it rather than in prose. Also confirmed: the\nfive consumers this item names all still branch on the vocabulary --\nAUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP, OPAQUE_BOUNDARIES, _DISCLOSED_ONLY_BOUNDARIES,\nDEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS (added since filing, by ADR-0049) and verify_claims'\nKNOWN_IO_BOUNDARIES check. DEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS is a sixth branching\nconsumer that did not exist when this was filed, which is the drift the item\npredicts."  # 0e7d
